<title>USA: TriMas sees record 1997 operating profit.</title>
<headline>TriMas sees record 1997 operating profit.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>TriMas Corp said Thursday it expects record operating profits for 1997, based on its outlook for continumed moderate economic growth this year.</p>
<p>The company also cited its ongoing cost-reduction, manufacturing efficiency and market share initiatives.  </p>
<p>TriMas today reported 1996 fourth quarter earnings of $0.40 per primary share, up from $0.35 a year ago. For the full year it earned $1.66 per primary share, up from $1.51 in 1995.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
